[h1]World Bridge[/h1]
Plan and fund massive crossings between islands and continents from your fortress.
Choose the shores directly on Dwarf Fortress's graphical world map.

[b]Requires DFHack. Development build: use a copied save.[/b]

[h2]How to use it[/h2]
1. Install DFHack. On Windows, use Steam DF 53.17 with DFHack 53.17-r1 or Steam DF 53.16 with DFHack 53.16-r3.
2. Subscribe, let Steam finish the download, and restart the game through DFHack.
3. Load a copied fortress save. Press Ctrl+Shift+D and run [code]world-bridge[/code]
4. Click land on each shore, review the route, create the project, and deliver blocks.

The Workshop download contains the working mod. No manual mod-file installation
or new world is required. You do not need to select it during world generation.
Use one installation method: remove an older manual copy before using Workshop,
since manual scripts can take priority over subscribed scripts.

[h2]Construction[/h2]
[b]100 blocks and 14 game days per water world tile.[/b] Shore tiles add no cost.
For example, three water tiles require 300 blocks and 42 days. Time starts after
full funding. Existing projects keep their saved costs and progress.

Completed crossings can materialize as elevated, three-wide local decks with
supports where their route intersects a loaded fortress map. The planner checks
terrain, water, headroom and existing construction before placement.

[h2]Travel[/h2]
Optional experimental raid routing guides assembled squads across verified
bridge routes and handles their return. Optional caravan access lets the native
game schedule traders from newly connected peaceful civilizations. Native seasons,
diplomacy and trade requirements still apply; enabling access does not summon a
caravan immediately. Other mission types and split armies are unsupported.

[h2]Controls[/h2]
W/A/S/D, arrows over the map, or middle drag: pan. Ctrl+C: center on fortress.
Ctrl+N: create. Ctrl+D: deliver. Ctrl+B: build or verify a local deck.
Ctrl+T: raid routing. Ctrl+E: caravan access. Ctrl+L: automatic local decks.
Ctrl+X: cancel an unfinished project or remove a completed bridge after confirmation.
Delivered blocks are spent. Completed bridge removal requires a clear, verified
deck and waits until guided squads and caravans are finished.
Esc closes the planner and leaves the native world map open.

[h2]Important limits[/h2]
This is version 0.5.0-dev. Use a copied save. Blocks are consumed, world records
remain after uninstalling, and local placement changes terrain beneath supports.
Land passability is approximated. Individual caravan world routes are not observed.
Do not unsubscribe during a guided squad trip. The planner uses the normal 1x map;
close World Map Zoom before opening it. Other DF/DFHack builds are not verified.

